{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed2085404187/4/prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"你是一个 ARC-AGI 谜题设计专家。下面的 20 道参考题是难度和机制质量的标杆。仔细阅读每道题的**解题逻辑**（解题者从样例归纳规则的认知过程），而非表面场景。你的新题应在机制深度和隐蔽性上与参考题持平或者实现超越。\n\n每个参考题描述包含：\n- `description`：一句话概述题目的变换目标。\n- `Input structure`：输入网格中有哪些对象、背景、标记、边界或组件。\n- `Rule`：从输入到输出的确定性变换规则。\n- `Key insight`：解题所需的核心洞见。\n\n参考题目如下：\n<reference_puzzle index=\"1\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"28a6681f\" lines=\"8-23\">\n<description>\nSimulate water pixels falling under gravity into basins formed by colored obstacles.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = 0. Water pixels = color 1 (blue).\n- Other colors form static solid structures (walls, steps, containers).\n- Water starts in unstable positions above or beside basins.\n\nRule:\n- Each water pixel falls straight down through bg cells.\n- When blocked below, it slides diagonally through the unique open side cell.\n- When resting on a surface, it slides horizontally toward the nearest gap where it can fall again.\n- Process repeats until no water pixel moves.\n\nKey insight: Water seeks the deepest reachable basin via diagonal and horizontal sliding, not just vertical fall.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a395ee82\" lines=\"9-24\">\n<description>\nStamp translated copies of a monochrome template guided by a singleton pixel layout.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. A large monochrome shape (template, color T).\n- Singleton pixels elsewhere: exactly one is color T (layout origin); the rest share color O (overlap color).\n- Singletons sit on a uniform-spacing lattice.\n\nRule:\n- Convert each singleton's offset from the origin into coarse lattice units.\n- Place a template copy at each offset, scaled by template height/width.\n- The origin's copy is painted O instead of T.\n- Any pixel covered by two or more copies is also recolored to O.\n\nKey insight: The single T-colored singleton identifies both the origin position and the \"self\" copy, which is uniquely recolored.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"3\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"5545f144\" lines=\"191-207\">\n<description>\nMove a triangular sprite across the grid, consuming aligned marker pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- Frames concatenated horizontally with solid divider columns; bg is most common color.\n- Each frame: a triangular arrow-shaped sprite and scattered single-pixel markers, all one color.\n\nRule:\n- Start from the rightmost frame.\n- At each step, exactly one cardinal direction from the head has reachable\n  markers (on a half-line: same row or column); the sprite advances to the\n  nearest one.\n- On reaching a marker, consume it; sprite re-faces that direction.\n- Repeat until no markers remain; output the final sprite position on a clean bg.\n\nKey insight: The triangle's tip encodes facing direction, which sets marker-consumption priority.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"4\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"6e4f6532\" lines=\"26-41\">\n<description>\nDock train sprites onto station groups by matching coupler count, then orient via divider-color markers.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg; colored stripes (edge + internal) partition grid into rectangular regions.\n- Color 8 forms train bodies; color 9 marks both isolated stations and train-attached couplers.\n- Stripe-colored pixels on trains are orientation markers.\n\nRule:\n- Stations = 8-connected 9-clusters not adjacent to any 8. Trains = components containing 8.\n- Match train to station group where |couplers| == |station size|.\n- Rotate/flip train so marker pixels face the same-color boundary stripe of the target region.\n- Translate so couplers align exactly onto station cells; erase original position.\n\nKey insight: Coupler count selects the docking target; marker color encodes which boundary stripe to face, fixing the unique orientation.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"5\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"f931b4a8\" lines=\"10-27\">\n<description>\nCount the two upper quadrant control regions to size an output made from the lower quadrant pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- The grid is an even square split into four equal quadrants.\n- Black is the background.\n- The upper-left and upper-right quadrants are control regions.\n- The lower-left quadrant is a color source tile; the lower-right quadrant is either a stencil tile or empty.\n\nRule:\n- Output height is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-left quadrant.\n- Output width is the number of non-background pixels in the upper-right quadrant.\n- If the lower-right stencil has foreground pixels, tile it over the output; each stencil background pixel is filled from the lower-left quadrant cell at the corresponding coarse tile position.\n- If the lower-right stencil is empty, tile the lower-left quadrant directly over the output.\n\nKey insight:\n- The top quadrants specify only dimensions, while the bottom quadrants specify a two-level repeated pattern: a fine stencil and coarse fill colors.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"6\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"58f5dbd5\" lines=\"20-34\">\n<description>\nCarve color-matched motifs into solid blocks and pack them into a compact grid.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Several solid 5×5 monochrome blocks, each a distinct non-bg color.\n- For each block color, a small same-colored motif sprite elsewhere on the grid.\n\nRule:\n- Match each motif to its same-colored 5×5 block.\n- Center the motif within the block and recolor those cells to bg (punching holes).\n- Pack all carved blocks into an output grid preserving their original row/column order, separated by 1-cell gaps and a 1-cell outer border.\n\nKey insight: The motif acts as a stencil — it's not stamped onto the block but carved out of it as background holes.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"7\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"97d7923e\" lines=\"81-94\">\n<description>\nRecolor vertical bars by legend-driven rank selection.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Top-left: monochrome blocks touching row 0; each has color K and height k.\n- Main grid: vertical bars capped top and bottom by a single color, with solid-color interiors.\n\nRule:\n- For each legend entry (K, k), find vertical bars capped by K.\n- Rank bars by interior length (longest = rank 1).\n- Recolor the rank-k bar's interior to K.\n\nKey insight: Legend height is a rank index into length-sorted bars, not a literal size.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"8\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"a47bf94d\" lines=\"178-189\">\n<description>\nTransmit colored tokens along wire networks, converting each to its complementary 3×3 pattern.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = background. Non-bg cells form wire networks and 3×3 tokens (solid blocks or X/diagonal patterns) near wire endpoints.\n\nRule:\n- Every solid 3×3 token is replaced in-place by a diamond (center + 4 cardinal neighbors).\n- Each token near a wire endpoint sends its complement to the opposite endpoint: solid emits X, X emits diamond.\n\nKey insight: Token shape cycles solid → X → diamond; wires route each complement to the far end.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"9\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b7bacbf\" lines=\"42-56\">\n<description>\nFill enclosed regions along a line seeded by unique border pixels.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- Colored lines/drawings on the grid.\n- Unique single-pixel colors on the grid border mark seed endpoints of each line.\n\nRule:\n- Each border seed pixel connects (8-connected) to a line drawing.\n- Find closed bg cavities whose boundary touches that line.\n- Flood-fill each such cavity with the seed pixel's color.\n\nKey insight: Only cavities reachable through the seed's own line get filled; the seed's unique color acts as a per-line fill label.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"10\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"7666fa5d\" lines=\"12-26\">\n<description>\nFill the parallelogram-shaped region between parallel anti-diagonal line segments with red.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color.\n- One non-bg color forms short diagonal segments, each lying on a single anti-diagonal (r+c = const).\n- Segments come in parallel pairs bounding a region to be filled.\n\nRule:\n- For each main-diagonal axis (r−c = const), collect anti-diagonal segments whose span covers that axis.\n- Sort those segments by their anti-diagonal index (r+c).\n- Fill all bg cells lying strictly between consecutive segment pairs along that axis with red (color 2).\n\nKey insight: The two diagonal directions decouple — segments sit on anti-diagonals, and filling sweeps along main diagonals between them, forming parallelogram regions.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"11\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"247ef758\" lines=\"35-46\">\n<description>\nMove colored sprites from the left strip into a framed area at marker-defined targets.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg background; rectangular frame on right with colored markers on its edges; sprites in a narrow left strip separated by a constant-color divider column.\n\nRule:\n- For each color, target rows/cols are where both opposite frame edges share that color. Targets are the Cartesian product.\n- Erase each sprite from the left and stamp it centered at every target. Higher sprites cover lower ones.\n\nKey insight: One sprite replicates to a grid of row × column marker intersections.\n</description>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle index=\"12\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"8b9c3697\" lines=\"9-23\">\n<description>\nInsert red components into interior sockets of large structures, leaving a black trail.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common. Large non-bg, non-red structures with interior cavities.\n- Red components outside structures.\n\nRule:\n- Interior sockets: bg cells inside a structure's bbox, adjacent to structure pixels.\n- For each structure, find the direction where rays from sockets hit a red component.\n- Slide that component into the socket; paint traversed cells black.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
